; Sprites: two-legged walker (4 frames), arms-up figure on a drum (4 frames)
;
; Eight 16x16 sprites of 32 bytes, 16 pixel rows of 2 bytes each (left byte, right byte; bit 7 = leftmost pixel). Sprite
; F of the page is at $AE00+32*F. Entity definitions (#R$A000) name the page in byte +5 and pick F from the animation
; phase, the direction and the slot data. The sprites are drawn with #R$9456 (#R$91BE) and have no colour of their own:
; ink and bright come from the entity definition. Frames 0-3 look like a flat-headed creature with two long legs
; stepping; frames 4-7 look like a figure with raised arms above a drum-like base, the arms waving. Used by entity
; definitions $26 $44 $5A $6A $6E in rooms $16 $20 $2B $2D $3C.
@label=SpritesWalkerDrum
